of  community in this show i feel like i'm  finally able to talk about this thing  completely because  volume two of season two finally did  come out we had to wait a long long time  for that because the first two didn't  sell up to expectations but finally  they did they threw the fans a bone and  they gave us this thing so i feel i can  do the whole scope  yes i understand there were more  episodes even after seasons two they  were called the goliath chronicles but  the creator of the show is just owned  them and generally they're not  considered canon so i'm not even gonna  deal with that but the progress of this  show i mean season one you immediately  just  by the fact that it delves right off the  bat  into this history and this depth of of  all this stuff going on in scotland and  the history of these characters  and then you get a lot of really bold  mysteries in the first season because  you get macbeth introduced who isn't  going to get explained for quite a while  but it is interesting right off the bat  john reese davies another voice shout  out i think  season 2 vol one is probably uh most of  my favorite stuff it just gets  really in-depth and we get a lot of  great stuff with the history of  demona and macbeth and you get to see  all these other characters just grow and  change and evolve  season two volume two i'm actually a  little bit iffy on because  it expands the world but it expands the  world  so much that it kind of makes the  gargoyles themselves seem  a little bit more minor in a weird way  because when the show  started the whole sort of hook and the  pitch was these gargoyles are the only  ones of their kind and the world that  they were once a part of is gone  well season two volume two material we  start finding out well there's avalon  there's other gargoyles  there's all these other sort of mystical  beings and the gargoyles themselves just  feel a little bit less special because  of that it's still great stuff don't get  me wrong but